  "steps": [
    "Pat the shrimp completely dry with paper towels, then season evenly with half of the kosher salt and all of the black pepper.",
    "Heat a 12-inch skillet over medium-high heat with olive oil and 1 tablespoon of butter for 2 minutes until the butter is melted and sizzling.",
    "Add the shrimp in a single layer and cook for 2 minutes without moving them, then flip and cook for 1 to 2 minutes more until opaque and pink throughout; transfer the shrimp to a clean plate.",
    "Reduce the heat to medium, add the remaining butter, minced garlic, and red pepper flakes to the same skillet, and sauté for 30 to 45 seconds until fragrant, taking care not to burn the garlic.",
    "Pour in the chicken broth and lemon juice, scraping up any browned bits from the bottom of the pan, and simmer for 1 minute.",
    "Add the spiralized zucchini noodles and the remaining salt to the skillet, tossing constantly over medium heat for 2 minutes until just tender-crisp and coated in sauce.",
    "Return the cooked shrimp and any accumulated juices back to the skillet, toss everything together for 30 seconds until heated through, garnish with fresh parsley, and remove from heat."
  ],
  "tips": [
    "Do not overcook the zucchini noodles or they will release too much water; keep the cooking time under 2 minutes.",
    "Patting the shrimp thoroughly dry is essential to get a proper sear instead of steaming them.",
    "Serve immediately as zucchini noodles continue to release moisture as they sit."
  ],
  "storage": "Best enjoyed immediately. Leftovers can be stored in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 1 day, though the zucchini will soften upon reheating.",
  "tools": [
    "12-inch skillet",
    "spiralizer",
